.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Clapeyron&#x27;s 1834 combined gas law unites Boyle&#x27;s law (PV constant at fixed T), Charles&#x27;s and Gay-Lussac&#x27;s law (V \propto T at fixed P), and Avogadro&#x27;s hypothesis into PV_m = RT. This example draws both classic views with IdealGas: hyperbolic Boyle isotherms, and straight Charles isobars that all extrapolate to zero volume at absolute zero.">

.. only:: html

  .. image:: /api/gallery/thermo/equations_of_state/images/thumb/sphx_glr_plot_01_ideal_gas_law_thumb.png
    :alt:

  :doc:`/api/gallery/thermo/equations_of_state/plot_01_ideal_gas_law`

.. raw:: html

      <div class="sphx-glr-thumbnail-title">Clapeyron's ideal gas law, PV = RT</div>
    </div>


