.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="van&#x27;t Hoff found that a dilute solution&#x27;s osmotic pressure (~chemistrykit.thermo.systems.mixtures.osmotic_pressure) equals the pressure the solute particles would exert as an ideal gas at the same concentration and temperature. The factor i counts particles per formula unit: 1 for sucrose, about 2 for NaCl. The same factor multiplies the other colligative effects, freezing-point depression and boiling-point elevation (~chemistrykit.thermo.systems.mixtures.freezing_point_depression, boiling_point_elevation).">

.. only:: html

  .. image:: /api/gallery/thermo/mixtures/images/thumb/sphx_glr_plot_03_osmotic_pressure_thumb.png
